{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSCWfjg5GASvDrJetVVx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A memory write no longer forces the next call to rebuild the whole system prompt in the cache. Only the new fact (about 15 tokens) gets written. I checked this offline with a fake client, not against the real API.\n\n**Cause:** `build_system()` sent everything in one cached text block: the instructions, today's date, the profile, the facts and the language line. Caching only reuses a prompt whose beginning matches exactly, so appending a fact changed that one block and the whole ~1000 tokens had to be written again. The language line also came after the facts, so a new fact landed in the middle of the prompt rather than at the end.\n\nSplitting the instructions into their own cached block wouldn't have worked. Tools plus instructions come to about 960 tokens, and Sonnet 4.5 needs at least 1024 before it caches anything. Below that it just silently doesn't cache.\n\n**Fix (`bot.py`):** the system prompt is now a list of blocks, with the parts that change most at the end:\n1. the instructions\n2. a new `athlete_profile()`: name, sport, zones, goal, language\n3. one block per fact, with the cache marker on the last one\n4. today's date, which isn't cached\n\nSince `save_fact` only ever appends, the old prompt is now an exact prefix of the new one. The API looks back up to 20 blocks for an earlier cached entry, so it reuses the old one and writes only the new fact. Two side effects:\n- The first message of each day no longer misses the cache because of the date.\n- I added a second cache marker on the profile block as a fallback, but it will probably do nothing: tools, instructions and profile together are likely just under the 1024 minimum.\n\n**Testing:** with a fake client I ran a reply that calls `save_fact`, then a second message. In each request, everything up to the previous cache marker was identical to the request before it. After deploying, rows right after a `save_fact` in `logs/usage.jsonl` should show a large `cache_read_input_tokens` and a small `cache_creation_input_tokens`.\n\n**Not fixed:** messages that match the plan or race keywords add tools, and tools sit before the system prompt, so those calls still miss the cache (the 1305 and 1334 rows). NOTES.md asks to keep the keyword filtering, so I left it; ANSWER.md describes an option if it matters.\n\nI also updated the caching sentence in README.md. Nothing is committed. I briefly put the test script in `/tmp/h-ndAPa2-test`, which is outside this directory; I deleted it afterwards."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":105,"cache_read_input_tokens":36981,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":105},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"74b98d88-e75f-4251-8df6-66bc69e54d9c","uuid":"7031a014-c2a0-4d8a-b342-a28430be5187","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:35:51.078Z","request_id":"req_011CgSCWfVoHDKWqx1eq5zWJ"}
